late, photo or specs) and the other car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Compare the permit, the plate and the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> with a note when they are different cars, or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b> when they are.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/similar-cars</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/460"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-06-similar-cars-desktop-562b0382.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="460"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.8%;top:30.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">From a listing, press <b class="gd-ui">The car and its rates</b>, or open the car from Field jobs.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the rates an Admin set. Only the daily rate is needed; the others follow from it when empty. The weekend rate is a price per day for each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> for the kilometres, or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check What renters pay under the fields, then press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>. Rates, kilometres and deposit save together.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-listings-and-covering-plates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Listings and covering plates</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting shows Needs review. Open it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself (change a line only if you must: it is then kept). Check the photos: on each public photo, cover the plate or mark it not visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/340"><img src="/guides/img/va-fleet-05-listings-desktop-d2672e0a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="340"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:54.5%;top:49.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="3"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The listing&#39;s Steps to go live says what is next: 1 Photos, 2 Cover plates, 3 Review, 4 Live on the site, each with its button. The plate box is suggested by itself on every outside photo as the listing opens (Box suggested). Press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> and check it; <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b> asks again. A photo filed under the wrong shot: <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it on the Photos card, then take the right one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box; drag a box to move it, its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/776"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-phone-95d5afd2.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="776"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:52.6%;top:78.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:43.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.5%;top:62.1%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:43.1%;top:92.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a photo whose plate is not checked stays private, and goes public by itself once it is covered or marked. The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-publish-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now</h2><p class="gd-p">Customer service and fleet publish a car themselves; nothing has to be finished first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the car from Listings or Field jobs. Its listing says why it is not on the site yet; press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. With no rates yet it uses the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is still open (paperwork, details, photos, No VIN yet for a car added by its plate, a possible duplicate) shows as warnings after Publish now and on the car. None of them stops publishing.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">New cars with their rates usually go on the site by themselves (Publish new cars automatically, on by default). A car taken off the site by staff waits for Publish now.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A car not on the fleet insurance policy yet can be requested, offered and paid for, but never handed over until the insurer confirms it. Requests and offers for such a car show a warning.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calendar sync with Turo and other platforms</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Calendar sync</b>: a car listed on Turo or Getaround must never be booked twice.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Turo has no calendar link: Turo&#39;s trip emails come in by themselves, find their car by themselves (Turo car number, plate, VIN, year, make, model, trim, colour, what earlier emails taught) and block it with the turnaround. Nothing to set up per car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An email the reader cannot place waits as &quot;Which car is this?&quot;: press <b class="gd-ui">Which car is this?</b> and press the right car (best guesses first). It is remembered for that car&#39;s next emails. If the dates or trip number are missing: <b class="gd-ui">Add as a Turo trip</b> (choose the car, check the dates) or <b class="gd-ui">Dismiss</b>. A trip whose email did not come: <b class="gd-ui">Add a Turo trip</b> on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each Turo trip shows the guest&#39;s name and phone when Turo&#39;s email includes them. Contact a Turo guest only about their trip, never with promotions.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Turo cannot read our calendar: under &quot;Block on Turo&quot;, block each CarmaCars booking on the car&#39;s Turo calendar, then press <b class="gd-ui">Done on Turo</b>. Dates that changed or a booking cancelled here show the dates to free on Turo.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Getaround, Google Calendar or another platform with a calendar (iCal) link: open <b class="gd-ui">Add a calendar link</b>, choose the platform, paste it and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the link</b>. Copy the car&#39;s CarmaCars link for that platform with <b class="gd-ui">Copy</b> and paste it into the platform&#39;s calendar import.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">A double booking raises an urgent task for you and an email: move, swap or cancel one trip. A link that stops working raises a task after 3 failed reads: copy it from the platform again.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Add the photos and readings</h3><p class="gd-p">A pickup or return recorded with the details later gives Fleet the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. Open the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-out (or check-in) photos and readings</b>: the usual checklist opens without the ready check or the renter&#39;s signature. Take the photos, the odometer, fuel, keys (and cleanliness at a return), sign and save. The task closes by itself; it cannot be closed by hand before.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-bookings-now" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rentals</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> opens on Now for fleet and customer service: the cars out with their renter and due-back countdown, coming back today and tomorrow (overdue first, in red), going out in the next 72 hours with what is ready, the money due in 7 days and the free cars. It refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. A booking listed as <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b> left without a check-out: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>, then add the photos, km and fuel from the task. The search above it finds any booking.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'photo-shoots', 'chapter', 'a-return', 'A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.

## Shoot the listing photos

1. Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press **I have read this**.
2. The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot (or **From photos** to pick one you took). **Retake** to redo one.
4. An upload failed? Press **Send again**. Then press **Submit for listing**. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Extra outside angles go under **More outside photos** (up to 20, placed on the studio background like the others) and extra inside or detail shots under **Other detail** (up to 20).

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg "phone; size: 390 730; pins: 1 89.7 34.2, 2 89.7 67.8, 3 29.0 97.3")

> Tip: Keep other cars'' plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car''s plate before the listing goes live.
', 'Photo shoots', 'Shoot a listing''s photos in order and submit them.',
  'A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.

## Shoot the listing photos

1. Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press **I have read this**.
2. The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.
3. Press **Take photo** for each shot (or **From photos** to pick one you took). **Retake** to redo one.
4. An upload failed? Press **Send again**. Then press **Submit for listing**. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Extra outside angles go under **More outside photos** (up to 20, placed on the studio background like the others) and extra inside or detail shots under **Other detail** (up to 20).

![](/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg "phone; size: 390 730; pins: 1 89.7 34.2, 2 89.7 67.8, 3 29.0 97.3")

The steps at the top say where the listing is: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in), 2 Cover plates, 3 Review and 4 Live on the site. Wrong shot? Press **Remove** under that photo, then **Remove it**, and take the right one. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

> Tip: Keep other cars'' plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car''s plate before the listing goes live.
',
  '<p class="gd-p">A photo shoot job gets a car ready for its listing. You shoot the list of photos with your phone and submit them for review.</p><section class="gd-task" id="photo-shoots-shoot-the-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Shoot the listing photos</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the photo shoot job and read the tips: daylight, a plain background, the phone held landscape. Press <b class="gd-ui">I have read this</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The shot list: each photo with a short description. The bar shows how many required photos you have.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Take photo</b> for each shot (or <b class="gd-ui">From photos</b> to pick one you took). <b class="gd-ui">Retake</b> to redo one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An upload failed? Press <b class="gd-ui">Send again</b>. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Submit for listing</b>. You can submit before every angle is done: the missing ones are listed under the button and can be added later. Extra outside angles go under <b class="gd-ui">More outside photos</b> (up to 20, placed on the studio background like the others) and extra inside or detail shots under <b class="gd-ui">Other detail</b> (up to 20).</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/730"><img src="/guides/img/field-06-photo-shoot-capture-phone-c0dae5b8.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="730"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.7%;top:34.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.7%;top:67.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29%;top:97.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">The steps at the top say where the listing is: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in), 2 Cover plates, 3 Review and 4 Live on the site. Wrong shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under that photo, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>, and take the right one. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Keep other cars&#39; plates out of the frame. The reviewer covers this car&#39;s plate before the listing goes live.</div></aside></section>');
